# Roadmap #30/#52 — types are first-class values.
# A value's type is read with `:` — `.` reads only the fields a type defines,
# and a value's type is not one of them. Types compare by identity with `==`.

x := i32 5,

same := x:type == i32,     # true: x was built as an i32
cross := x:type == f64,    # false: i32 is not f64
meta := i32:type == type,  # true: a type's own type is the `type` root

same and meta and not (cross)
